  "body": "The longer we leave the https://whatwg.github.io/streams/ URL out there, the more people will start linking to it, which is bad since I meant it only as a convenient stopgap while I figured out the server config necessary to get it to its final destination.\n\nTagging in @annevk @Hixie for help:\n\nThe deployment should of course be automatic. Right now the deployment is done via Travis CI and [this script](https://github.com/whatwg/streams/blob/master/deploy-gh-pages.sh) which pushes to gh-pages (which GitHub reflects as the github.io URL automatically). I like this workflow, especially since it fails the push if the reference implementation tests fail. So if there is a way to push data to the WHATWG servers I'd love that.\n\nAlternately we could set up a post-test hook that invokes a script on the WHATWG servers that then pulls the data.\n",
